    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for a chili that tastes like it took a lot more effort than it did. Canned pumpkin is one of the cheapest thickeners on the shelf and it brings fiber along with it.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBuy plain canned pumpkin, not pie filling.\u003c/strong\u003e The pie filling is already sugared and spiced and it costs more. You want the one with a single ingredient on the label.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eCocoa powder is a savory ingredient too.\u003c/strong\u003e A container lasts years and a spoonful of it is what separates a good chili from a flat one. Same idea as a mole.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eStock up on canned pumpkin in November.\u003c/strong\u003e It is the one month of the year the price bottoms out, and the cans are good for a very long time.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eFrozen chopped spinach disappears into chili.\u003c/strong\u003e It costs less than fresh, it will not go bad on you, and nobody eating it will notice it is in there."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Cook the rice separately per the package and set it aside covered.",
                    "Brown the ground turkey in your big pot over medium-high heat, breaking it up until it is cooked through.",
                    "Add the diced onion and chopped green bell peppers and cook until soft, then stir in the garlic for the last minute.",
                    "Stir in the chili powder, cocoa powder, ground cinnamon, ground cumin, cayenne, salt and black pepper and toast them against the hot pan for a minute.",
                    "Add the canned pumpkin puree, the tomato paste, the diced tomatoes with their juice and the chicken broth, and stir until the pumpkin is fully blended into the base.",
                    "Add the drained cannellini beans, simmer 30 minutes, then stir in the thawed chopped spinach at the end. Keep the sour cream and cilantro for topping at reheat."
                ],
